Cortex is a Rust workspace with crates under `crates/`:

- `cortex`: core agent logic, providers, sessions, extensions
- `cortex-cli`: the `cortex` binary (CLI, `serve`, recipes, schedules)
- `cortex-providers` / `cortex-provider-types`: model provider implementations and shared wire types
- `cortex-context-management`: conversation compaction and summarisation
- `cortex-mcp`: bundled MCP servers
- `cortex-sdk` / `cortex-sdk-types`: SDK bindings and protocol types
- `cortex-agent` / `cortex-local-inference` / `cortex-download-manager` / `cortex-roaming`: agent runtime, local inference, model downloads, P2P transport
- `cortex-test` / `cortex-test-support`: test harness and fixtures

`ui/desktop` is the Electron app (TypeScript + React). It talks to the backend over ACP
through the workspace package `@cortex/acp-client` in `ui/acp-client`.

Non-trivial behaviour belongs in the `cortex` crate and is exposed to the CLI through
`cortex-cli`. The desktop app calls the backend over ACP; do not import generated
OpenAPI client code from `ui/desktop/src/api`.

Tips:

- Check unstaged changes to see what is currently being worked on.
- Always verify `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and run the tests
  in the files you touched.
- In `ui/desktop`, run `pnpm run typecheck` and the tests for the files you touched.